## Building on Linux

```sh
make clean && make && make test
```

## Building on Windows (MSYS2 UCRT64)

**Recommended:** open **MSYS2 UCRT64** from the Start menu:

```sh
pacman -S make mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-gcc   # once
cd /path/to/true-toto
make clean && make && make test
```

Produces a **native Windows executable** (`true-toto` or `true-toto.exe`).
Runs in UCRT64, Git Bash, and CMD.

### Git Bash caveat

Git Bash can build if **`/c/msys64/ucrt64/bin` is early on `PATH`** (before
Anaconda). Otherwise `gcc --version` may work while `cc1` fails silently (DLL
load order). Prefer UCRT64 shell or:

```bash
PATH="/c/msys64/ucrt64/bin:$PATH" make
```

## Linking notes

- Tests link `src/true_toto_cli.c` and `src/true_toto_emit.c` directly to
  access `scan_meta_flags()` — no special inline-header trick is needed.
- `main()` lives only in `src/main.c` and is **never** linked into the test
  binary.
- There is no `static inline` helper shared between the main binary and tests;
  all testable logic is in normal `.c` translation units.

